text:
alex: heads-up i'm flipping the convo_schema_toggle for a small canary. quick sanity check: how does this affect streaming tool-call timing and the final payload for non-streaming clients?

jia: older SDKs that only parse `delta` chunks might ignore `event_type` values they don't know. they usually skip unknown event types, but some client code does strict unions. :eyes:

miriam: important: we didn't change `messages[].role` normalization, still 'system'|'user'|'assistant'. the toggle moves tool payloads out of `delta.content` into distinct `tool_call` events in stream mode. for non-streaming we add a `tool_calls` array in the final body.

sam: PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/runtime/pull/1234 — implements `event_type: "tool_call"` streaming chunks and final `tool_calls` summary. added unit + e2e tests.

alex: thanks. couple of specific asks: 1) will clients that assume `content` is always a string break if they see `content_chunks`? 2) do we need a per-route opt-out?

jia: we kept `messages[].content` as a string for backwards compat — `content_chunks` is optional and only present for very large splits. so naive parsers still get a string in `content`. if someone was deserializing raw stream events by type only, they should be fine.

miriam: per-route opt-out is doable with a flag in route config. default is preserved. we should add a migration note for Dedicated customers.

alex: @deploy-bot can you start a 10% canary in us-west-2 for 30m? want to watch tool-call latency.

deploy-bot: deploybot: starting canary: runtime-v2.3.1-canary (convo_schema=true) -> canary 10% in us-west-2. monitor: http://ci.internal/redwood/canary/4987654321 :rocket:

qa-bot: quick question — if client sets `stream: false`, do we still provide tool_call results inline? some integrations expect synchronous tool outputs.

miriam: yes. non-streaming: `200 OK` body includes `tool_calls: [ { name, args, result } ]` and `messages` containing final assistant message. streaming: intermediary `tool_call` events + final summary.

sam: one gotcha: some older clients parse streaming deltas and immediately append `delta.content` to the UI. they may see an extra event with `event_type: tool_call` and try to render a big JSON blob. recommend SDKs filter `tool_call` events unless they opt-in to tool UI. added note in PR.

alex: action items: @sam update SDK changelog and add filtering helper; @jia write migration blurb for clients; @miriam add a Dedicated config guide; i'll watch the logs for 30m and surface any errors.

deploy-bot: canary metrics @ t+20m: error-rate 0.12% (baseline 0.09%). increased latency for requests involving tool_call by ~120ms median. some timeouts in downstream tool adapters. pausing ramp to 0% pending investigation.

alex: roll it back to 0% for now. post findings in this thread. :thumbsup:

sam: root cause identified: streaming seq-num off-by-one when convo_schema=true causes tool_call reassembly to drop the first chunk. fix in PR 1236 (small patch). will re-run canary after patch.

jia: i'll draft the migration note and include suggested client-side filtering snippet, e.g.:
```
// pseudo-sdk snippet
client.onEvent(e => {
  if (e.event_type === 'tool_call') {
    // skip rendering by default
    return;
  }
  renderDelta(e);
}
)
```

miriam: sounds good. after sam's patch + another short canary let's ship the toggle wider.

alex: great. we'll sync in the weekly api-compat slot if anything else crops up. thanks everyone. :white_check_mark:
